G54: polled side keys (boot-arg g54keys=1).

Volume up is MTK KPD 0x1c00e000 KP_MEM1 bit 0; power and volume down are
MT6363 TOPSTATUS 0x1e bits 1 and 3, read over SPMI through the AP's PMIF
software channel (SWINF 2 at PMIF 0x1c804000 + 0x880, as the stock
spmi-mtk-pmif.ko selects for MT6855). Offsets from the stock
mtk-pmic-keys.ko and spmi-mtk-pmif.ko, checked live by the g54-xnu probe
(E27). A thread polls every 20 ms with a two-sample debounce and reports
through sweet_hid_key(). It also acknowledges MT6363 interrupts like the
stock PMIC IRQ handler (status write-back, 0x41b = 1): without that one
power press cold-resets the phone ~79 s later (E30/E31). Off by default.

